{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J26muxomzbkVhY4BYFn647","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tlayout: default\n3\ttitle : \"Overture.Operations module (The Agda Universal Algebra Library)\"\n4\tdate : \"2022-06-17\"\n5\tauthor: \"the agda-algebras development team\"\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t### Operations\n9\t\n10\tThis is the [Overture.Operations][] module of the [Agda Universal Algebra Library][].\n11\t\n12\tFor consistency and readability, we reserve two universe variables for special\n13\tpurposes.\n14\t\n15\tThe first of these is `𝓞` which we used in the [Overture.Signatures][]\n16\tas the universe of the type of *operation symbols* of a signature.\n17\t\n18\tThe second is `𝓥` which we reserve for types representing *arities* of relations or\n19\toperations.\n20\t\n21\tThe type `Op` encodes the arity of an operation as an arbitrary type `I : Type 𝓥`,\n22\twhich gives us a very general way to represent an operation as a function type with\n23\tdomain `I → A` (the type of \"tuples\") and codomain `A`.\n24\t\n25\t<!--\n26\t```agda\n27\t{-# OPTIONS --cubical-compatible --exact-split --safe #-}\n28\t\n29\tmodule Overture.Operations where\n30\t\n31\t-- Imports from Agda and the Agda Standard Library -----------------------------\n32\topen import Agda.Primitive               using () renaming ( Set to Type )\n33\topen import Level                        using ( Level ; _⊔_ )\n34\t\n35\t-- Imports from the Agda Universal Algebra Library -----------------------------\n36\topen import Overture.Signatures          using ( 𝓥 )\n37\t\n38\tprivate variable a b ρ : Level\n39\t```\n40\t-->\n41\t\n42\t```agda\n43\t-- The type of I-ary operations on A.  Arity first, carrier second, so that\n44\t-- `Op (Fin 2)` partially applies as \"the type of binary operations\" on any given A.\n45\tOp : Type 𝓥 → Type a → Type (a ⊔ 𝓥)\n46\tOp I A = (I → A) → A\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tFor example, the `I`-*ary projection operations* on `A` are represented as\n50\tinhabitants of the type `Op I A` as follows."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47e5a51d-6a73-420a-8866-36d226ccb1e5","uuid":"1cd32014-b00a-40eb-815a-111c88a73b98","timestamp":"2026-09-26T03:31:36.484Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/nix/store/0mkdwhwzshgsa7xknd81r8hvdp6gbmr6-agda-algebras-unstable-2026-09-07/src/Overture/Operations.lagda.md","content":"---\nlayout: default\ntitle : \"Overture.Operations module (The Agda Universal Algebra Library)\"\ndate : \"2022-06-17\"\nauthor: \"the agda-algebras development team\"\n---\n\n### Operations\n\nThis is the [Overture.Operations][] module of the [Agda Universal Algebra Library][].\n\nFor consistency and readability, we reserve two universe variables for special\npurposes.\n\nThe first of these is `𝓞` which we used in the [Overture.Signatures][]\nas the universe of the type of *operation symbols* of a signature.\n\nThe second is `𝓥` which we reserve for types representing *arities* of relations or\noperations.\n\nThe type `Op` encodes the arity of an operation as an arbitrary type `I : Type 𝓥`,\nwhich gives us a very general way to represent an operation as a function type with\ndomain `I → A` (the type of \"tuples\") and codomain `A`.\n\n<!--\n```agda\n{-# OPTIONS --cubical-compatible --exact-split --safe #-}\n\nmodule Overture.Operations where\n\n-- Imports from Agda and the Agda Standard Library -----------------------------\nopen import Agda.Primitive               using () renaming ( Set to Type )\nopen import Level                        using ( Level ; _⊔_ )\n\n-- Imports from the Agda Universal Algebra Library -----------------------------\nopen import Overture.Signatures          using ( 𝓥 )\n\nprivate variable a b ρ : Level\n```\n-->\n\n```agda\n-- The type of I-ary operations on A.  Arity first, carrier second, so that\n-- `Op (Fin 2)` partially applies as \"the type of binary operations\" on any given A.\nOp : Type 𝓥 → Type a → Type (a ⊔ 𝓥)\nOp I A = (I → A) → A\n```\n\nFor example, the `I`-*ary projection operations* on `A` are represented as\ninhabitants of the type `Op I A` as follows.","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":65}}}
